WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.660
The panel says Live, updated 0 s ago.

2
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:11.990
The measurement was observed ten minutes ago. Both are true.

3
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:17.430
Source, collector, API, browser: four timelines.

4
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:26.490
Collector samples every 10 min. Browser polls every 30 s.

5
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:32.970
19 polls, 19 × 200 OK, before the collector samples again.

6
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.680
Every response carries the same reading, collectedAt 00:00:00.

7
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:40.620
Response freshness: served just now.

8
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:46.510
Measurement freshness: observed at 00:00:00. Live reports only the first.

9
00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:53.930
Fix: measurement age from sourceObservedAt; connection from the last poll.

10
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:59.130
Connected and stale can both be true.

11
00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:05.600
Advance the shared clock. The source value does not change.

12
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.480
Polls succeed. Nothing resets the age.

13
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:16.610
30 s, 60 s … 330 s: past this fixture's 300 s stale policy, still 200 OK.

14
00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:20.800
Five minutes is this dashboard's policy, not a universal rule.

15
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:28.110
Collector down: API still 200, age 1200 s, connection green.

16
00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:36.890
API down: 503. Last value kept with an explicit warning. Nothing invented.

17
00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.430
Freshly fetched does not mean freshly observed.

18
00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:48.560
Polling faster or a WebSocket delivers the same old reading sooner.
